WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
Spearmint and caraway smell nothing alike.

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:08.030
Yet each smell comes from a compound
with the same name: carvone.

3
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.710
The two carvone molecules are
mirror images of each other.

4
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.630
Same atoms, same bonds,
even the same boiling point.

5
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.010
So how can your nose tell them apart?

6
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.870
In this mission, you'll meet cis–trans
isomers, and find the chiral carbons,

7
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:27.630
bonded to four different groups, that
make mirror-image molecules possible.

8
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.510
You'll see how each mirror-image
form rotates plane-polarized light,

9
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.590
and what happens in a racemic mixture.

10
00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.240
Your mission: explain how your nose
tells mirror-image molecules apart.
